ble-filterfns","text":"Variable: filterFns","level":1},{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"arrhas","text":"arrHas","level":3},{"id":"arrincludes","text":"arrIncludes","level":3},{"id":"arrincludesall","text":"arrIncludesAll","level":3},{"id":"arrincludessome","text":"arrIncludesSome","level":3},{"id":"between","text":"between","level":3},{"id":"betweeninclusive","text":"betweenInclusive","level":3},{"id":"empty","text":"empty","level":3},{"id":"endswith","text":"endsWith","level":3},{"id":"equals","text":"equals","level":3},{"id":"equalsstring","text":"equalsString","level":3},{"id":"equalsstringsensitive","text":"equalsStringSensitive","level":3},{"id":"includesstring","text":"includesString","level":3},{"id":"includesstringsensitive","text":"includesStringSensitive","level":3},{"id":"indaterange","text":"inDateRange","level":3},{"id":"innumberrange","text":"inNumberRange","level":3},{"id":"notempty","text":"notEmpty","level":3},{"id":"startswith","text":"startsWith","level":3},{"id":"weakequals","text":"weakEquals","level":3},{"id":"deprecated","text":"Deprecated","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# ~~Variable: filterFns~~\n\n```ts\nconst filterFns: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts:442](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts#L442)\n\nThe built-in filter function registry.\n\nRegistering this full object opts out of tree-shaking: every built-in\nfilter function ends up in your bundle. Prefer importing the `filterFn_*`\nfunctions you actually use and registering just those in the `filterFns`\nslot, or passing them directly to the `filterFn` column option.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### ~~arrHas~~\n\n```ts\narrHas: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrHas;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludes~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludes: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludes;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludesAll~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludesAll: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludesAll;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludesSome~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludesSome: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludesSome;\n```\n\n### ~~between~~\n\n```ts\nbetween: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_between;\n```\n\n### ~~betweenInclusive~~\n\n```ts\nbetweenInclusive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_betweenInclusive;\n```\n\n### ~~empty~~\n\n```ts\nempty: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_empty;\n```\n\n### ~~endsWith~~\n\n```ts\nendsWith: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_endsWith;\n```\n\n### ~~equals~~\n\n```ts\nequals: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equals;\n```\n\n### ~~equalsString~~\n\n```ts\nequalsString: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equalsString;\n```\n\n### ~~equalsStringSensitive~~\n\n```ts\nequalsStringSensitive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equalsStringSensitive;\n```\n\n### ~~includesString~~\n\n```ts\nincludesString: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_includesString;\n```\n\n### ~~includesStringSensitive~~\n\n```ts\nincludesStringSensitive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_includesStringSensitive;\n```\n\n### ~~inDateRange~~\n\n```ts\ninDateRange: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_inDateRange;\n```\n\n### ~~inNumberRange~~\n\n```ts\ninNumberRange: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_inNumberRange;\n```\n\n### ~~notEmpty~~\n\n```ts\nnotEmpty: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_notEmpty;\n```\n\n### ~~startsWith~~\n\n```ts\nstartsWith: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_startsWith;\n```\n\n### ~~weakEquals~~\n\n```ts\nweakEquals: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_weakEquals;\n```\n\n## Deprecated\n\nImport individual `filterFn_*` functions instead for a smaller\nbundle. This export still works and is not going away in v9, but built-in\nname resolution (including `filterFn: 'auto'`) only finds functions you\nregister yourself.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: filterFns\ntitle: filterFns\n---\n\n# ~~Variable: filterFns~~\n\n```ts\nconst filterFns: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts:442](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts#L442)\n\nThe built-in filter function registry.\n\nRegistering this full object opts out of tree-shaking: every built-in\nfilter function ends up in your bundle. Prefer importing the `filterFn_*`\nfunctions you actually use and registering just those in the `filterFns`\nslot, or passing them directly to the `filterFn` column option.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### ~~arrHas~~\n\n```ts\narrHas: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrHas;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludes~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludes: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludes;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludesAll~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludesAll: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludesAll;\n```\n\n### ~~arrIncludesSome~~\n\n```ts\narrIncludesSome: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_arrIncludesSome;\n```\n\n### ~~between~~\n\n```ts\nbetween: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_between;\n```\n\n### ~~betweenInclusive~~\n\n```ts\nbetweenInclusive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_betweenInclusive;\n```\n\n### ~~empty~~\n\n```ts\nempty: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_empty;\n```\n\n### ~~endsWith~~\n\n```ts\nendsWith: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_endsWith;\n```\n\n### ~~equals~~\n\n```ts\nequals: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equals;\n```\n\n### ~~equalsString~~\n\n```ts\nequalsString: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equalsString;\n```\n\n### ~~equalsStringSensitive~~\n\n```ts\nequalsStringSensitive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_equalsStringSensitive;\n```\n\n### ~~includesString~~\n\n```ts\nincludesString: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_includesString;\n```\n\n### ~~includesStringSensitive~~\n\n```ts\nincludesStringSensitive: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_includesStringSensitive;\n```\n\n### ~~inDateRange~~\n\n```ts\ninDateRange: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_inDateRange;\n```\n\n### ~~inNumberRange~~\n\n```ts\ninNumberRange: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_inNumberRange;\n```\n\n### ~~notEmpty~~\n\n```ts\nnotEmpty: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_notEmpty;\n```\n\n### ~~startsWith~~\n\n```ts\nstartsWith: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_startsWith;\n```\n\n### ~~weakEquals~~\n\n```ts\nweakEquals: CreatedFilterFn<any, any> = filterFn_weakEquals;\n```\n\n## Deprecated\n\nImport individual `filterFn_*` functions instead for a smaller\nbundle. This export still works and is not going away in v9, but built-in\nname resolution (including `filterFn: 'auto'`) only finds functions you\nregister yourself.\n"}
